---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { analysisMedia as media, analysisCaptures as captures } from '../showcases/grounded-analysis/content';
---
<section class="analysis-showcase wrap" id="analysis-in-context" aria-labelledby="analysis-showcase-heading" data-grounded-analysis>
  <div class="analysis-intro">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Actual extraction, fictional conversation</p><h2 id="analysis-showcase-heading">The names passed.<br /><em>The meaning still needs review.</em></h2></div>
    <p>A real analysis saved seven statements from a fictional notebook conversation. One kept the storage choice. Another turned a project-specific preference into a general one.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="analysis-editorial-label">Editorial review after the run <span>Two selected statements, reproduced unchanged.</span></p>
  <div class="analysis-comparisons">
    <article class="analysis-comparison analysis-supported" aria-labelledby="analysis-supported-title">
      <p class="analysis-verdict">Supported in this transcript</p><h3 id="analysis-supported-title">The storage choice stayed intact.</h3>
      <p class="analysis-saved-label">Actual saved statement</p><p class="analysis-triple"><strong>Harbor Notebook</strong><span>uses</span><strong>IndexedDB</strong></p>
      <p class="analysis-source-label">Authored fictional source</p><blockquote>“Keep IndexedDB as the primary store for Harbor Notebook.”</blockquote>
      <p>The stored relationship agrees with the source’s explicit storage choice.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="analysis-comparison analysis-review" aria-labelledby="analysis-review-title">
      <p class="analysis-verdict">Project scope was lost</p><h3 id="analysis-review-title">A qualification disappeared.</h3>
      <p class="analysis-saved-label">Actual saved statement</p><p class="analysis-triple"><strong>Mira Vale</strong><span>prefers</span><strong>manual file export</strong></p>
      <p class="analysis-source-label">Authored fictional source</p><blockquote>“I prefer manual file exports over cloud sync <mark>for this project</mark>: I want to choose when a copy leaves the tablet.”</blockquote>
      <p>The saved statement drops the project boundary. The name validator accepted it; it did not catch this meaning error.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="analysis-review-note">These are editorial comparisons made after extraction. The saved output remains unchanged. No automatic semantic correction is demonstrated.</p>
  <details class="analysis-detail analysis-validation">
    <summary>What the name checks caught <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div>
      <p class="analysis-trace-label">Recorded validation trace <span>One job. Three real provider requests.</span></p>
      <ol class="analysis-trace" aria-label="Selected recorded name-resolution checks">
        <li><span class="analysis-step">01</span><div><h3>Resolve proposed names</h3><p>Mira Vale / Harbor Notebook / IndexedDB</p><p>The local runtime recorded those proposals.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="analysis-step">02</span><div><h3>Reject uncovered forms</h3><p><code>mira</code> / <code>harbor notebook</code> / <code>indexeddb</code></p><p>Nine coverage violations rejected the first submission.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="analysis-step">03</span><div><h3>Accept the repaired submission</h3><p>Mira Vale / Harbor Notebook / IndexedDB</p><p>The model restored the resolved names in the same job. Seven statements were saved.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p>This compact trace selects names from the actual saved execution records. The catalog started empty, so this run demonstrates required resolution coverage, not reuse of an existing alias. Passing the checks did not establish semantic accuracy.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <div class="analysis-film-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Check the wording</p><h3>Open the source conversation.</h3></div><p>The actual UI recording starts at the entity profile, after analysis has completed. The link opens the conversation; it does not cite an exact message.</p></div>
  <figure class="analysis-film">
    <video controls playsinline preload="none" poster={`${media}/entity.png`} width="1440" height="1000" aria-label="Actual PanelForge entity profile opens the authored fictional source conversation after analysis" aria-describedby="analysis-film-scope">
      <source src={`${media}/source-navigation.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
      <track kind="captions" src={`${media}/source-navigation.vtt`} srclang="en" label="English action captions" default />
      <p><a href={`${media}/source-navigation.mp4`}>Open the source-navigation film</a></p>
    </video>
    <figcaption id="analysis-film-scope"><strong>Actual PanelForge UI after a real analysis of an authored fictional transcript.</strong> GPT-OSS 120B via OpenRouter/Cerebras produced the saved analysis. The transcript’s Codex model and CLI labels are fictional source metadata, and its notebook implementation claims are fictional.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="analysis-film-links"><a href={`${media}/source-navigation.mp4`}>Open the 7-second film full size <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a><a href={`${media}/source-navigation.vtt`}>Read the action captions <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div>
  <p class="analysis-editing">The opening search is omitted. The remaining seven seconds retain the original speed, loading wait and navigation. Sidebar and message metadata are masked; the source wording is unchanged.</p>
  <fieldset class="analysis-captures">
    <legend>Inspect the source views</legend>
    <div class="analysis-choices">{captures.map(capture => <label><input type="radio" name="analysis-capture" value={capture.id} checked={capture.id === 'entity'} /><span>{capture.label}</span></label>)}</div>
    <div class="analysis-frames">{captures.map(capture => <figure data-analysis-frame={capture.id}>
      <a class:list={['analysis-image-link', {'analysis-phone': capture.id === 'phone'}]} href={`${media}/${capture.file}`} aria-label={`Open full-size ${capture.label} capture`}><img src={`${media}/${capture.file}`} alt={capture.alt} width={capture.width} height={capture.height} loading="lazy" /><span>Open full size <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a>
      <figcaption><strong>{capture.title}</strong><span>{capture.caption}</span></figcaption>
    </figure>)}</div>
  </fieldset>
  <details class="analysis-detail analysis-method"><summary>Source, model and capture limits <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div>
    <p>On 15 October 2026, two field-authored fictional exchanges were imported through PanelForge’s actual JSONL importer and projector. One analysis job, picked up once, made three HTTP requests through the registered GPT-OSS 120B profile. It resolved candidates, rejected an uncovered submission and accepted the model’s repair. No response or desired triple was injected.</p>
    <p>The unchanged application source was <code>web-v10.20.97</code>. The accepted model triples matched the persisted fields, and source-event bytes and message identities remained unchanged. The UI links identify the conversation as a whole. Editorial source quotations on this page do not create message-level product citations.</p>
    <p>The registered requests pinned Cerebras, disabled fallbacks and requested ZDR. Returned routing metadata identified the selected provider and model. This is routing evidence, not an independent provider-retention guarantee. The source receipt separates requested controls from observed facts.</p>
    <p>The source viewer displays a read-only badge but exposes enabled edit controls. They were not used, and the private harness blocked writes. The footage does not establish a shipped read-only UI. The phone source was reached through its entity event button; the bottom conversation-list button was occluded. Dashboard question and event counters are not used to measure the accepted arrays here.</p>
    <p>The app was freshly compiled in an isolated fixture. External font CSS was fulfilled locally with an empty stylesheet, so these captures use fallback fonts. The static Forge branding and app/model icons remain. No private catalog or live service is connected to this portfolio page.</p>
    <a href={`${media}/receipt.json`}>Read the selected execution receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a><a href="/work/knowledge-graph/">See the Memory case study <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
  </div></details>
</section>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-grounded-analysis]').forEach(section => {
    const video = section.querySelector('video');
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => video?.pause());
  });
</script>
<style>
.analysis-showcase{padding-block:22px 52px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:28px}.analysis-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;align-items:end;gap:26px 60px;margin-bottom:30px}.analysis-intro .eyebrow,.analysis-film-heading .eyebrow{font-size:14px;color:var(--rust);margin-bottom:14px}.analysis-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4.1vw,4rem);line-height:1.1}.analysis-intro h2 em{color:var(--forest)}.analysis-intro>p{font-size:18px;line-height:1.8;max-width:470px;color:var(--muted)}
.analysis-editorial-label{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;font-weight:650;margin-bottom:15px}.analysis-editorial-label>span{font-weight:400;margin-left:18px;color:var(--muted)}.analysis-comparisons{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border:1px solid #b6c1ac;border-top:4px solid var(--forest)}.analysis-comparison{padding:25px 28px;background:#edf0e4;min-width:0}.analysis-review{border-left:1px solid #b6c1ac;background:#f4e9dd}.analysis-verdict{font-size:14px;font-weight:650;color:#375039;margin-bottom:12px}.analysis-review .analysis-verdict{color:#843b25}.analysis-comparison h3{font-size:27px;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:25px}.analysis-saved-label,.analysis-source-label{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}.analysis-source-label{margin-top:24px}.analysis-triple{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:5px 11px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7}.analysis-triple strong{font-weight:650}.analysis-triple>span{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);border-bottom:1px solid #9eaa95}.analysis-comparison blockquote{margin:0;padding-left:15px;border-left:2px solid #99a88c;font-size:17px;line-height:1.8}.analysis-review blockquote{border-color:#b76d51}.analysis-comparison mark{background:#f0d2ae;color:#64311f;padding:1px 3px}.analysis-comparison>p:last-child{font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin-top:16px}.analysis-review-note{font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin:16px 0 28px;max-width:850px}
.analysis-detail{border-block:1px solid var(--line)}.analysis-detail>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;min-height:56px;padding:14px 4px;font-size:16px;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}.analysis-detail[open]>summary :global(.ui-icon){transform:rotate(45deg)}.analysis-detail>div{padding:10px 0 24px}.analysis-detail p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--muted);max-width:920px;margin-bottom:14px}.analysis-detail code{font-size:14px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.analysis-trace-label{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px 18px}.analysis-trace-label>span{color:var(--ink)}.analysis-trace{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:18px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border:1px solid #bdc8b3;background:#edf0e4}.analysis-trace li{display:flex;gap:14px;padding:20px;min-width:0}.analysis-trace li+li{border-left:1px solid #bdc8b3}.analysis-step{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);padding-top:3px}.analysis-trace h3{font:650 17px/1.5 var(--sans);margin:0 0 10px}.analysis-trace p{font-size:14px;margin:0 0 6px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.analysis-film-heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.15fr;gap:24px 50px;align-items:end;margin:38px 0 23px}.analysis-film-heading h3{font-size:29px;line-height:1.25}.analysis-film-heading>p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted);max-width:560px}.analysis-film{margin:0}.analysis-film video{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:1440/1000;background:#151b23;border:1px solid #84957a;border-radius:4px}.analysis-film video::cue{font-size:clamp(14px,1.6vw,24px);color:white;background:#101820}.analysis-film figcaption{padding-top:16px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.85;max-width:940px;color:var(--muted)}.analysis-film figcaption strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:650}.analysis-film-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:3px 30px;margin:7px 0 12px}.analysis-film-links a,.analysis-method a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:46px;font-size:15px}.analysis-editing{font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:28px;max-width:850px}
.analysis-captures{min-width:0;padding:24px 0 0;border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:0}.analysis-captures legend{float:left;width:100%;font-size:17px;font-weight:650;margin:0 0 14px;padding:0}.analysis-choices{clear:both;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px;margin-bottom:18px}.analysis-choices label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:46px;padding:10px 18px;border:1px solid #84957a;border-radius:3px;cursor:pointer;font-size:15px}.analysis-choices input{width:17px;height:17px;flex-shrink:0;margin:0;accent-color:var(--forest)}.analysis-choices label:has(:checked){color:var(--paper);background:var(--forest-dark);border-color:var(--forest-dark)}.analysis-choices label:has(:checked) input{accent-color:var(--paper)}.analysis-choices label:has(:focus-visible){outline:3px solid var(--rust);outline-offset:4px}.analysis-frames figure{margin:0;min-width:0}.analysis-image-link{display:block;background:#151b23;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none}.analysis-image-link img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.analysis-image-link>span{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:46px;padding:10px 16px;color:#e5e9ec;font-size:14px;border-top:1px solid #39444c}.analysis-phone{max-width:390px;margin-inline:auto}.analysis-frames figcaption{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.6fr;gap:12px 36px;padding:18px 0 28px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.85}.analysis-frames figcaption strong{font-size:17px;font-weight:650}.analysis-frames figcaption>span{color:var(--muted)}.analysis-captures:has([value=entity]:checked) [data-analysis-frame]:not([data-analysis-frame=entity]),.analysis-captures:has([value=source]:checked) [data-analysis-frame]:not([data-analysis-frame=source]),.analysis-captures:has([value=phone]:checked) [data-analysis-frame]:not([data-analysis-frame=phone]){display:none}.analysis-method a{margin-right:28px}.analysis-showcase :is(a,summary):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--rust);outline-offset:4px}
@media(max-width:760px){.analysis-showcase{padding-block:8px 40px}.analysis-intro,.analysis-film-heading{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.analysis-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.15rem,8vw,3.3rem)}.analysis-intro>p{font-size:17px}.analysis-editorial-label>span{display:block;margin-left:0}.analysis-comparisons{grid-template-columns:1fr}.analysis-comparison{padding:22px 20px}.analysis-review{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #b6c1ac}.analysis-comparison h3{font-size:25px}.analysis-trace{grid-template-columns:1fr}.analysis-trace li+li{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #bdc8b3}.analysis-film-heading{margin-top:30px}.analysis-film-heading h3{font-size:27px}.analysis-film video:not(:fullscreen)::cue{font-size:14px}.analysis-film-links{gap:0}.analysis-choices{gap:8px}.analysis-choices label{padding:10px 13px}.analysis-frames figcaption{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}.analysis-film figcaption{font-size:16px}}
</style>
